  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 339112) has seen $1.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Total award activity includes 10,876 awards with an average award size of $97.6K. Obligations fell 34.1% year over year. Fiscal-year trends show a peak at $2.3B in FY21, declines to $1.1B in FY22, recoveries to $1.5B in FY23 and $2B in FY24, and a decline to $1.6B in FY25 before returning to $1.1B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer with $899M in obligations so far this year. The Department of Defense follows with $68M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $61.5M. The vendor list is led by SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC at $194M, FIRST NATION GROUP LLC at $103M, and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC at $90.1M. Contracting officers and small business teams should weigh VA demand and the concentration among a few large vendors when planning capture and partnership strategies.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "The market recorded obligations down 34.1% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows variability, with obligations at $2.3B in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $2B in FY24, $1.6B in FY25, and $1.1B in FY26. Buyers and award cadence drove the swings, led by large VA activity in the current year. Program funding timing and multi-year procurements likely explain the peaks and troughs."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who concentrates buying and supply in this NAICS?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs concentrates buying with $899M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense and the Department of Health and Human Services follow with $68M and $61.5M respectively. Vendor concentration is visible, with SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC at $194M and FIRST NATION GROUP LLC at $103M leading suppliers. Smaller agency buys and many single awards make up the remainder of the $1.1B total."
      }
    ]
  },
